        "original_id": "84c26fc5-6284-5609-8239-e582e7c0c30e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Madeline Rees George\n- Organizations: Adelaide High School, Advanced School for Girls, Adelaide Girls' High School\n- Places: Germany, South Australia, Adelaide Parklands\n- Topics: Teaching, school leadership, government secondary education\n\nFacts:\n- Madeline Rees George, often written M. Rees George, was born around 1851 and died on 17 June 1931.\n- Madeline Rees George was a teacher in Germany and in South Australia.\n- Madeline Rees George was at various times the proprietor of her own school.\n- Madeline Rees George was headmistress of the Advanced School for Girls and Adelaide Girls' High School.\n- Adelaide High School is a coeducational state high school on the corner of West Terrace and Glover Avenue in the Adelaide Parklands.\n- Adelaide High School was the first government high school in South Australia.",
